@page "/"

<PageTitle>ZodSharp Blazor sample</PageTitle>

<h1>ZodSharp Blazor sample</h1>
<p>
	The same <code>[ZodSchema]</code> models from <code>Examples.Shared</code> validate in every render mode. Each page
	shows one way to use them.
</p>
<ul>
	<li>
		<a href="orders">Interactive Server</a>: the standard <code>&lt;DataAnnotationsValidator /&gt;</code> (route 1)
		over a nested address, a collection of lines and a dictionary of addresses, with field-level validation.
	</li>
	<li>
		<a href="register">Interactive WebAssembly</a>: <code>&lt;ZodValidator&gt;</code> (route 2) with debounced
		validation, error codes, an async uniqueness check and server errors mapped back onto the form.
	</li>
	<li>
		<a href="returns">Static SSR</a>: a posted form with client-side validation of ZodSharp rules
		(<code>[StartsWith]</code>, <code>[UUID]</code>) before it is submitted.
	</li>
</ul>
<p>Switch the language above to see the validation messages in French; codes and paths never change.</p>
